/Title (The furnace is composed of a deionized water-cooled copper coil. When energized with an AC power source, it develops an electromagnetic field. Any metal charge kept inside the crucible is subjected to electromagnetic induction. The electromagnetic field creates eddy currents in the charge, causing an opposite circulating stirring flow of electrons within the molten mass. This generates heat in the charge depending on its resistivity, without flames and without touching the material. Gas combustion furnaces carry inherited deficiencies that compromise anode performance. Electromagnetic induction removes them. The difference shows up in anode lifespan, processing time, and worker safety.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3545 0 R
/Next 3566 0 R
>>
endobj
